\section{Pairing palettes with a mood}{

The light moods share their ground with the lightest colors of several
palettes (the creams of \code{cafe} and \code{paz}, the light centers of the diverging
palettes, the pale ends of the sequential ones). That is natural for filled
areas such as heatmaps, where the center then reads as neutral, but those
colors fade when used for points or lines. The \code{guerra} mood uses the indigo
that starts \code{guerra} and \code{guerra_azul}, so pair it with other palettes, for
example \code{paz} or \code{sofia}: the ground of War with the colors of Peace.
}

